    - Out of scope
        - DAG-based formal causal inference (do-calculus, backdoor criterion, instruments). Pearl's full framework belongs in a later chapter or a sidebar; this chapter is correct to stay at the inquiry-loop level.
        - Reanalysis of the actual 1975 Berkeley dataset. Synthetic two-department version is the right pedagogical choice.
        - Multilevel models with more than two segments and continuous covariates. Chapter 11 territory.
        - Lord's paradox, ecological fallacy, and other related but distinct phenomena. Worth a one-line forward pointer at most.
        - Frequentist tests for the existence of Simpson reversal (Cornfield conditions, etc.). Out of scope for an inquiry-style chapter.
        - Changes to the expkit hierarchical_segmented_posterior implementation. The model is fine; only the chapter's claims about it need adjustment.
